  "classification_notes": [
    "Upstream invalid verdicts are mandatory denials. Valid metadata is evaluated against field types, RFC edition and explicit local policy independently of the tested implementations.",
    "The initial exploratory adapter missed a duplicate-key policy classification for key-generated.json#172 (a,a=1). Both production implementations already denied it. The adapter was corrected after inspecting the pinned source; no production code changed.",
    "Dictionary cases preserve original field lines. Opaque-parameter cases remove only outer SP, prepend a valid algorithm member plus a probe parameter, and preserve the remaining original bytes. Commas and multiline item/list framing are excluded to avoid changing their interpretation.",
    "Digest fields reference RFC 8941. RFC 9651 Date and Display String types are outside this field edition. Inner lists are not parameter values; preference members require integers from zero to ten.",
    "The synthetic probe parameter counts toward the 256-parameter limit. Byte limits include the complete adapted field value. Duplicate dictionary members are explicitly classified from the two pinned duplicate cases; opaque duplicate parameters remain permitted.",
    "This checks acceptance and rejection, not generic structured value decoding or serialization. Existing transport integration is covered by the selected digest regression suites."
  ],
